# Native v1.37 full-source research measurements

Final acceptance remains reconstructed Rust with whole-original byte identity. None of these native research artifacts is accepted as a contract replacement.

The complete native candidate11 source map matches all812 files in the retained Linux source map. A Darwin/arm64 v1.37 source build nevertheless produces raw SHA256 `d1189b77…`,707,992 bytes, versus the retained Linux build's `3bbaf27f…`,707,448 bytes. The candidate11 Utilize window `[236632,241736)` agrees under the existing precisely defined call/relocation normalization. Across the whole program,1,241 inferred windows have normalized correspondences; unmatched runtime windows and raw ELF/data differences remain. These are comparison-method results, not recovery percentages or exhaustive semantics.

The initial native attempt failed before completion because Clang could not find `assert.h`. The corrected attempt supplies the installed macOS SDK via `SDKROOT` and a host-only `-isysroot` flag. Its logs and frozen driver are retained. This is an explicit research setup adaptation, not attribution of the target's historical build recipe.

Subsequent cached full-source builds test justified local Rust control-flow forms without modifying the compiler profile, injecting assembly, changing metadata flags or supplying captured instructions as build inputs. The frozen source deltas, complete source maps, commands, actual compiled binaries and logs are retained. `native-experiments.json` classifies complete entry-bounded Utilize windows; none equals the target even under call/relocation normalization. Negative results apply to this native environment and do not exclude different output in the canonical Linux environment.

The compiler-IR diagnostic build uses `--emit=llvm-ir,link -Csave-temps`; its entire raw executable is identical to the corresponding ordinary native negative-guard build. The retained handler IR shows two separate blocks writing error86 and branching to the same cleanup. Source changes that expose one shared error, tail result, positive admission, Option/Result admission, deferred method comparison and pattern matching have measured negative outcomes. Repeated source forms that collapse to identical executables are kept as controls rather than counted as independent repairs.

The official Linux and native archives report the same Rust/Cargo/newlib source commits, but all20 target-library filenames/hashes differ between their sysroot maps. A separately cloned private native toolchain with the Linux target sysroot overlaid compiled the original812-file source map to exactly the same native executable. This is the measured result; it does not identify the remaining phase responsible for the Linux/native difference. The native compiler's source, flags and target libraries must not be called a uniquely recovered original recipe.

`verify.py` checks retained files, actual ELF hashes, source/log bindings, exact one-file source changes and the complete window classifications. It needs no compiler, VM or network. Original captures and immutable Linux comparison artifacts remain external hash-bound inputs. The large compiler archives, toolchains and build targets remain local research cache, not vendored sources.
